-- Interpretation Act 1965 (Singapore): INDEPENDENT TESTS.
-- Written by an author who decided every expected value from the source text (ANSWERS.md) before opening this module's siblings.
-- Scenario numbers (S<n>, B<n>) refer to ANSWERS.md. Expected values are never copied from a run.
-- A failing assertion is a finding and is left failing.
-- The encoding's convention for "the Act does not say" is NOTHING (or, in the seat, the sentence "The Interpretation Act does not say.").
-- Test helpers only (no rule of the Act is restated here):

GIVEN w IS A STRING
      part IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`names of word include` w part MEANS
    any (GIVEN n YIELD CONTAINS n part) (`what the Act names in defining` w)

GIVEN w IS A STRING
      part IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`words of word contain` w part MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Act's words defining` w
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST s THEN CONTAINS s part

GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF STRING
      part IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a list of text has an item containing` xs part MEANS
    any (GIVEN s YIELD CONTAINS s part) xs

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE STRING
      part IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the maybe text contains` m part MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST s THEN CONTAINS s part

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE Moment
GIVETH A MAYBE Moment
`test helper: the same moment in UTC` m MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (`the moment on the UTC clock` x)


-- s 1, s 54, s 55
#ASSERT `this Act binds the Government` -- S2 s 55
#ASSERT NOT (`the Act affects the rights of the Government` FALSE FALSE) -- S3 s 54
#ASSERT `the Act affects the rights of the Government` TRUE FALSE -- S4 s 54
#ASSERT `the Act affects the rights of the Government` FALSE TRUE -- S5 s 54

-- s 2(1) lead-in, s 2(2), s 2(2A)
#ASSERT `the definitions in section 2(1) apply to a written law enacted on` (Date 1 1 1950) -- S6 s 2(1) lead-in
#ASSERT `the definitions in section 2(1) apply to a written law enacted on` (Date 1 1 2030) -- S7 s 2(1) lead-in
#ASSERT NOT (`the definitions in section 2(1) affect a thing done on` (Date 27 12 1965)) -- S8 s 2(1) lead-in
#ASSERT `the definitions in section 2(1) affect a thing done on` (Date 28 12 1965) -- S9 s 2(1) lead-in
#ASSERT `a variant of a defined word has a corresponding meaning in that law` `a cognate expression` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S10 s 2(2)
#ASSERT `a variant of a defined word has a corresponding meaning in that law` `a cognate expression` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- S11 s 2(2) contrary intention
#ASSERT `the definition a written law provides applies` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- S12 s 2(2A)
#ASSERT `the definition a written law provides applies` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- S13 s 2(2A)

