-- GAPS: scenarios the encoding has no function for (reason after each).
-- GAP S1 s 1: the short title is not an encoded value; no function returns it
-- GAP S17 s 2(1) "act": no function decides whether a given omission is within a definition; the table records only what the Act names
-- GAP S19 s 2(1) "act": no function tells whether a definition applies in a given context (a contract); the table has no such input
-- GAP S22 s 2(1) "Act": negative membership (an Act of Malaysia without force of law) has no function
-- GAP S23 s 2(1) "Act": negative membership (a UK Act) has no function
-- GAP S30 s 2(1) "animal": whether an inclusive definition decides an insect (NOT COVERED) has no function
-- GAP S33 s 2(1) "Attorney-General": negative membership (an unassigned Deputy) has no function
-- GAP S34 s 2(1) "Attorney-General": negative membership (the Solicitor-General) has no function
-- GAP S35b s 2(1) "Deputy Attorney-General": negative membership (appointed some other way) has no function
-- GAP S36b s 2(1) "citizen of Singapore": negative membership (only a Malaysian citizen) has no function
-- GAP S38b s 2(1) "common law": negative membership (a custom without force of law) has no function
-- GAP S39b s 2(1) "Commonwealth country": negative membership (a country not recognised) has no function
-- GAP S41 s 2(1) "Commonwealth country": negative membership (a colony is not a Commonwealth country) has no function
-- GAP S45 s 2(1) "consular officer": negative membership (an honorary trade commissioner) has no function
-- GAP S47b s 2(1) "court": negative membership (a court in Malaysia; a court lacking jurisdiction) has no function
-- GAP S52 s 2(1) "export": negative membership (a move within Singapore) has no function
-- GAP S53c s 2(1) "import": negative membership (taking out of Singapore) has no function
-- GAP S56c s 2(1) "Gazette": negative membership (a newspaper notice) has no function
-- GAP S57 s 2(1) "Government": negative membership (the Government of Malaysia) has no function
-- GAP S58b s 2(1) "Government Printer": negative membership (an unauthorised printer) has no function
-- GAP S61 s 2(1) "Sovereign": the definition is stated only "in relation to the United Kingdom"; no function takes the country
-- GAP S68 s 2(1) "Judge": negative membership (a District Judge) has no function
-- GAP S71b s 2(1) "Judicial Service Officer": negative membership (a Legal Service officer) has no function
-- GAP S77b s 2(1) "master": instance membership (a captain; a person temporarily in charge) has no function
-- GAP S81 s 2(1) "monogamous marriage": negative membership (polygamous, involuntary, unrecognised, same-sex) has no function
-- GAP S82b s 2(1) "month": negative membership (a fixed 30 days) has no function
-- GAP S85 s 2(1) "oath": the limit "for persons allowed by law to affirm" has no input; the table cannot say a person who may not affirm is NOT COVERED
-- GAP S87b s 2(1) "Ordinance": negative membership (a Proclamation without force of law) has no function
-- GAP S89 s 2(1) "Parliament": negative membership (the Parliament of Malaysia) has no function
-- GAP S92b s 2(1) "police officer": negative membership (a Royal Malaysia Police officer) has no function
-- GAP S93b s 2(1) "prescribed": negative membership (subsidiary legislation under a different Act) has no function
-- GAP S95 s 2(1) "prescribed": negative membership (a website not specified) has no function
-- GAP S98 s 2(1) "public holiday": negative membership (a day informally observed) has no function
-- GAP S99 s 2(1) "public holiday": negative membership (a Sunday as such) has no function
-- GAP S100b s 2(1) "public officer": negative membership (unpaid post; private employee) has no function
-- GAP S102b s 2(1) "registered": negative membership (an unrelated law) has no function
-- GAP S109 s 2(1) "sign": the limit "a person unable to write his or her name" has no input; NOT COVERED for one who can write has no function
-- GAP S111 s 2(1) "Singapore": negative membership (a place first administered on 3 June 1959) has no function
-- GAP S112 s 2(1) "States of Malaya": a count of the named States has no function (the table keeps the list as one phrase)
-- GAP S116 s 2(1) "States of Malaya" (b): negative membership (a Federal Territory formed from Sabah) has no function
-- GAP S118 s 2(1) "statutory declaration" (a): negative membership (in Singapore before a notary, not under that Act) has no function; the table has no "where made" input
-- GAP S122b s 2(1) "statutory declaration" (c): negative membership (a person with no authority) has no function
-- GAP S124 s 2(1) "subsidiary legislation": negative membership (a circular without legislative effect) has no function
-- GAP S125b s 2(1) "United Kingdom": negative membership (the Republic of Ireland; the Isle of Man) has no function
-- GAP S133 s 2(1) "writing": NOT COVERED for an audio recording has no function
-- GAP S159 s 2(5): the word used ("give", "send") is not an input; nothing to ask
-- GAP S185 s 2A(5)/(6): the function takes "an organ is to be removed" without distinguishing the two named Acts from any other Act, so the case of removal under some other Act cannot be asked
-- GAP S190 s 2A(7): the Minister power to prescribe the criteria by regulations is not encoded as a function
-- GAP S191 s 2A(7)(b): the Minister power to prescribe qualifications and form is not encoded as a function
-- GAP S210 s 8(1)(a)(iii): the 1 March 2021 cut-off is a yes/no input ("published before 1 March 2021"), so the boundary date cannot be tested
-- GAP S211 s 8(1)(a)(iii): same: the 1 March 2021 cut-off is an input, not computed
-- GAP S221 s 9A(1): whether the purpose is expressly stated is not an input; nothing to ask
-- GAP S225 s 9A(2)(b): the purposes offered are only the three permitted ones; "to depart from a clear, non-absurd ordinary meaning" cannot be asked
-- GAP S286 s 22: no input for the date the instrument is to take effect; "before the passing" cannot be asked
-- GAP S306 s 28(2): the function is about dismissal only; "suspension" cannot be asked of it, so the silence on suspension is not representable
-- GAP S317 s 32: the declared date is not an input; the function returns the one permitted date, so a declared date before the appointee began to act cannot be asked
-- GAP S325 s 32A(2)(a): a body whose number is neither fixed nor within a range is not representable: the function treats every non-fixed body as within (ii)
-- GAP S338 s 33A(b): the function has one combined output; an activity unrelated to hedging cannot be asked
-- GAP S339 s 33A: the effect of a Minister direction depends on its content; the function treats any direction as removing the default
-- GAP S359 s 36(5)(c): conditions inconsistent with the nature of the function cannot be asked; the feature is offered only as the permitted kind
-- GAP S397 s 41A(7): the Minister power to prescribe by order in the Gazette is not encoded as a function
-- GAP S443 s 43: whether the evidence is only prima facie (rebuttable) is not modelled
-- GAP S448b s 46(1): an order that is not published in the Gazette cannot be asked (no input for publication)
-- GAP S455 s 47: the event (retirement) is not an input; the silence on retirement is not representable
-- GAP S467 s 48(9): the appointed date is an input (it is the commencement of s 2 of another Act); nothing to ask
-- GAP S468 s 48(8): the Minister power to make regulations is not encoded as a function
-- GAP S481c s 49: a distance measured along the road (NO) cannot be asked: the function only says the straight-line rule applies
-- GAP S488 s 10(1)(a): there is no "in operation at this instant" predicate; the instant of commencement is asserted in S487a
